Z||000000||Brian87egotrip||08-26-2001||08:54 AM||||Are they worth it? any type better than the other? I am putting a 3.1 in my 87 gt and I am thinking about headers. Are the fiero store's any good? Thanks for the help. Brian  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||08-26-2001||09:19 AM||||The general consensus is that the Fiero Store "headers" (they're really just fancy manifolds) are worth just a few horsepower. (Seems like 3-4.) About as much as porting the stock manifolds. Unmodified stock manifolds are very restrictive. <BR>Several folks have used FOCOA or West Coast headers with decent results. Maybe other brands.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||08-26-2001||10:50 AM||||Hey Brian!<BR>That is a can of worms you have opened up...<BR>It all depends on the headers you buy or have built, and the built ones are better than most prefab headers, although they cost more too!<BR>If you are looking for bottom end torque and decent HP, then you want headers with small diameter primary tubes that are long (over 18 inches)...<BR>But if you want gobbs of upper rpm HP with low bottom end torque, large diameter primaries that are short (zoomie tubes as used on a dragster) fill the bill...<BR>Course, I am only touching on the subject, as there are other factors that come into play as well...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
